<h1>Michelle N. Pierre</h1>
<p>Chicago Board of Education, District 1b, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.votemichellepierre.com" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (votemichellepierre.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Pierre says she is running to strengthen schools through experienced leadership, empower families with real choices and clear information, and ensure policies reflect the needs of every child, not just a few in the right neighborhoods. She describes her campaign as powered by people, not special interests, and rooted in experience, integrity, and understanding of the district&#39;s communities.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>An education professional with roughly 20 to 30 years in public education, she has been described in local coverage as a former charter network leader and former chief academic officer of the Cleveland Metropolitan School District. She ran for the District 1B seat in 2024, losing to Jennifer Custer.</p>
